  "implementation": [
    "QAM Registry owns its actual full Vec slot capacity and live status String capacities followed by an existing Retained guard. Initial/replacement candidates reserve before publication; no mutable Deref bypass exists.",
    "Selected Snapshot aliases keep their existing independent archive/wrapper/root guards. Registry replacement clones only finite status/Arc handles; actual candidate capacity is measured without assuming clone/growth capacity.",
    "Performance Entry guards already include each live fixed slot and all children. Retained Vecs normalize through boxed slices to capacity==len, clear drops the whole Vec, and insertion normalizes under the store lock before publication. No duplicate live-entry charge or new registry framework.",
    "Initial performance Begin admits complete Entry and QAM candidates before replacing either old history. Host rejection after Entry admission preserves both previous registries and returns unstarted dispatch admission through existing Model behavior.",
    "Existing lifecycle fixtures include actual QAM initial/current reservations; historical scientific, coordinate, null, original-byte and final-alias assertions stay intact. Fixed Store/Context/Vec handles and presentation/infrastructure remain separate pending owners.",
    "Public APIs, scientific algorithms, native bindings, schema, Cargo dependencies and CXX/QML registration remain unchanged."
  ],
